source: tests/help_pages.rs
description: "a command's -h and --help pages as this build renders them at 100 columns without color; any change to an about, a flag, a value, a heading or the layout changes them: review with cargo insta review, or re-accept with INSTA_UPDATE=always cargo test --test integration help_pages:: and review git diff tests/snapshots/"
---
==> omaddons backup verify -h <==
Check backups against their recorded hashes

Usage: omaddons backup verify [OPTIONS] <ID>...

Arguments:
  <ID>...  The backups: ids, or prefixes of 8 or more characters

Examples:
  omaddons backup verify 01M6Q2VA            check it against its hashes
  omaddons backup verify 01M6Q2VA --dry-run  check it, recording nothing

Global: -t <TARGET>  --json  --dry-run  -v  --quiet  --no-color  --offline  (--help lists them all)
==> omaddons backup verify --help <==
Check backups against their recorded hashes

A backup without hashes gets a first baseline recorded instead.

Usage: omaddons backup verify [OPTIONS] <ID>...

Arguments:
  <ID>...
          The backups: ids, or prefixes of 8 or more characters

Examples:
  omaddons backup verify 01M6Q2VA               check it against its hashes, or record them
  omaddons backup verify 01M6Q2VA 01M6Q8PN -t retail
  omaddons backup verify 01M6Q2VA --dry-run     check, record nothing

Hashes every file of a backup and compares it with the hashes it recorded when it was
captured with --verify, imported, or verified before. A backup without hashes gets them
recorded now, as a first baseline: later checks then catch any change, but this cannot
prove the capture itself was intact, and the output says so. A file that differs makes
the backup damaged, which backup restore then refuses. Nothing else changes.

See also: backup list, backup create

Global options:
      --json             One JSON envelope on stdout
      --format <FORMAT>  Output format [possible values: json, human]
  -t, --target <TARGET>  The client to act on: id, game mode, family, path, or all [alias: --flavor]
      --dry-run          Show the plan without changing anything
      --actor <ACTOR>    Who is acting: human, agent or widget [env: OMADDONS_ACTOR]
      --reason <TEXT>    Why, recorded verbatim in history
      --offline          Fail any network access [env: OMADDONS_OFFLINE=1]
      --while-running    Allow folder changes while the client runs (never SavedVariables)
      --no-color         No ANSI color
      --no-progress      No progress output
      --progress <MODE>  Progress events on stderr [possible values: json, human, none]
      --quiet            Only errors on stderr
  -v, --verbose...       More detail (repeatable)
  -h, --help             Show help

Learn more: omaddons robot-docs guide
